<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Detailed Prompting of SwiftSolve</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The detailed prompting schema of the Planner, Coder, Profiler, and Complexity Analyst are shown in Figure <a href="#A2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Appendix B Example Dataset Schema ‣ SwiftSolve: A Self-Iterative, Complexity-Aware Multi-Agent Framework for Competitive Programming" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, <a href="#A2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Appendix B Example Dataset Schema ‣ SwiftSolve: A Self-Iterative, Complexity-Aware Multi-Agent Framework for Competitive Programming" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, <a href="#A2.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Appendix B Example Dataset Schema ‣ SwiftSolve: A Self-Iterative, Complexity-Aware Multi-Agent Framework for Competitive Programming" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, and <a href="#A2.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix B Example Dataset Schema ‣ SwiftSolve: A Self-Iterative, Complexity-Aware Multi-Agent Framework for Competitive Programming" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, respectively. Additionally, we visualize the competitive programming problem schema input and output for SwiftSolve, noted in Figure <a href="#A2.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix B Example Dataset Schema ‣ SwiftSolve: A Self-Iterative, Complexity-Aware Multi-Agent Framework for Competitive Programming" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a> and <a href="#A2.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Appendix B Example Dataset Schema ‣ SwiftSolve: A Self-Iterative, Complexity-Aware Multi-Agent Framework for Competitive Programming" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>, respectively.</p>
</div>
</section>
